      "body": "## Overview\n\nThis PR enables Octave KV (`ROCM_OCTAVE`) on gfx1151 (Strix Halo, RDNA3.5).\n\nUpstream currently allows Octave only on gfx942 and gfx1100, so `--kv-cache-dtype octave_*` can't run on gfx1151. To try it, I modified the build and kernel dispatch to accept gfx1151, then ran `vllm bench` on real hardware. This PR contains those changes and the results.\n\n[#59774](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/59774) reports that, on 4x RX 7900 (gfx1100), Octave stores 4.6x more KV tokens than fp16 and matches its GSM8K accuracy, with `octave_k3v3` scoring 92.4 against 91.8 for fp16. Those are its numbers, not mine. The results below are the gfx1151 measurements.\n\nI'm aware that RDNA3 (gfx1100) and RDNA3.5 (gfx1151) are different architectures, so the gfx1100 results don't automatically carry over to gfx1151. I'm opening this PR for enablement: it makes Octave available on gfx1151 using the existing kernels, not tuned for RDNA3.5.\n\n\n## Claims\n\n- Octave KV builds, serves and completes all benchmark requests on gfx1151 (0 failed), using the\nexisting gfx1100 WMMA kernels unc\n- Preliminary, pending the correctness check: at 100k input, TTFT is 4.3x lower and output\nthroughput about 4.5x higher thannd at 8k input with 16 concurrentrequests, output throughput is about 1.9x higher.\n- At 8k input with 1 concurrent rhan the baseline (6.2-7.0 against8.8 tok/s), because the baseline benefits from working MTP.\n- TODO: KV capacity compared with\n- TODO: accuracy compared with the baseline.\n\n## Validation\n\n**Hardware and software**\n\n- Device: TODO (e.g. Ryzen AI Max+ 395, gfx1151, VRAM allocation)\n- ROCm / PyTorch: TODO\n- Commit: TODO\n- Model: cyankiwi/Qwen3.8-27B-AW\n\n**Build**\n\n```bash\n# TODO: build command, including the VLLM_GPU_ARCHES / HIP target used\n```\n\n**Serving**\n\nThe baseline omits `--kv-cache-dtype octave_k3v3` or `octave_k3v4`.\n\n```bash\nvllm serve cyankiwi/Qwen3.8-27B-AWQ-INT4 \\\n  --dtype float16 \\\n  --kv-cache-dtype octave_k3v3 \\ # Or octave_k3v4 in k3v4 benchmark\n  --tensor-parallel-size 1 \\\n  --max-model-len 131072 \\\n  --max-num-seqs 6 \\\n  --max-num-batched-tokens 2048 \\\n  --language-model-only \\\n  --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"qwen3_next_mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":3}'\n```\n\n**Benchmark**\n\n```bash\nMODEL=cyankiwi/Qwen3.8-27B-AWQ-INT4\nTAG=octave_k3v3 # Or octave_k3v4 in k3v4 benchmark\n\nrun() {\n  vllm bench serve \\\n    --model $MODEL \\\n    --dataset-name random \\\n    --random-input-len $1 \\\n    --random-output-len 512 \\\n    --ignore-eos \\\n    --seed 0 \\\n    --num-prompts $2 \\\n    --max-concurrency $3 \\\n    --percentile-metrics ttft,tpot,itl,e2el \\\n    --save-result --result-filename bench_${TAG}_${1}_c${3}.json\n}\n\nrun 8000   6  1\nrun 32000  4  1\nrun 100000 3  1\nrun 8000   64 16\n```\n\n**Results on gfx1151 (all requests completed, 0 failed)**\n\n| Input len | Concurrency | KV cache | Mean TTFT (s) | Mean TPOT (ms) | Output tok/s | MTP acceptance |\n| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 8k | 1 | baseline | 19.4 | 75.6 | 8.82 | 88.9% |\n| 8k | 1 | `octave_k3v3` | 15.8 | 129.5 | 6.24 | 0.0% |\n| 8k | 1 | `octave_k3v4` | 16.1 | 111.4 | 7.02 | 5.3% |\n| 32k | 1 | baseline | 101.9 | 224.5 | 2.36 | 70.9% |\n| 32k | 1 | `octave_k3v3` | 55.8 | 114.1 | 4.49 | 4.3% |\n| 32k | 1 | `octave_k3v4` | 56.8 | 106.3 | 4.61 | 7.0% |\n| 100k | 1 | baseline | 624.6 | 576.5 | 0.56 | 78.1% |\n| 100k | 1 | `octave_k3v3` | 145.9 | 110.6 | 2.53 | 5.5% |\n| 100k | 1 | `octave_k3v4` | 145.9 | 112.9 | 2.51 | 4.6% |\n| 8k | 16 | baseline | 741.1 | 782.5 | 6.69 | 61.9% |\n| 8k | 16 | `octave_k3v3` | 371.7 | 429.6 | 12.63 | 2.5% |\n| 8k | 16 | `octave_k3v4` | 373.9 | 421.7 | 12.75 | 4.4% |\n\n**KV capacity:** TODO: GPU KV cache size from the server logs for each configuration.\n\n**Accuracy**\n\nTODO: GSM8K on gfx1151 for the baseline and each Octave mode.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- `CMakeLists.txt`: build the Octave sources when `VLLM_GPU_ARCHES` includes gfx1151.\n- `csrc/attention/octave_decode_wmma_rdna3.cu`, `csrc/attention/octave_prefill_rdna3.cu`: compile the WMMA kernels for gfx1151 instead of stubs, and dispatch gfx1151 to the same tier as gfx1100.\n\n\n**Duplicate check:** I found no open PR targeting Octave on gfx1151 or Strix Halo.\n\n**AI assistance:** AI assistance was used for this PR. I reviewed every changed line and ran the benchmarks above.\n\n---",
